# ---------------- TK_Bullet.events (Task 16 Part H + C.5) ----------------
# TK4 projectile: flies along the shooter's facing at the weapon's speed, knocks the victim
# back with the weapon's knockback, then dies — or bounces off a wall, or explodes on it.
#
# The scene's "Bullet", "ShotgunPellet", "UziBullet" and "Rocket" actors are only templates for
# `spawn Bullet at me`: `spawn` swaps in the held weapon's `<Weapon>Bullet` name, so the clone
# is a pellet, an uzi round or a rocket. The spawner also stamps the weapon's data onto every
# clone — `my BulletSpeed`, `my Life`/`my TimeLeft`, `my damage`, `my knockback`, `my blast`
# and the `my Bounce` / `my Explosive` / `my Pierce` flags (see WeaponData.events) — so this
# one sheet serves every weapon. A template that was never spawned reads 0 and sits still.

# --- flight: 400 cm/s crosses ~12 m over its 3 s life, TK4's reach across the screen;
#     a rocket is slower and a shotgun pellet has short legs. ---
when every 0 seconds
  my BulletSpeed is higher than 0
  move forward speed my BulletSpeed

# --- lifetime: `Life` is stamped too. `when every` takes a literal, so count it down in
#     fixed steps instead of arming one timer per bullet. ---
when every 0.25 seconds
  my BulletSpeed is higher than 0
  add -0.25 to my TimeLeft
  if my TimeLeft is lower than 0
  destroy me

# --- walls (Part C.5): bounce back, blow up, or just stop ---
when me touches wall
  if my Bounce is true
  bounce
  otherwise
  if my Explosive is true
  explode
  otherwise
  destroy me

# --- enemies: the weapon's own damage and knockback; rockets burst, piercers carry on ---
when me touches Enemy
  if my Explosive is true
  explode
  otherwise
  # `for 0.2 seconds` keeps shoving, so the knockback is visible instead of a single frame.
  push other back strength my knockback for 0.2 seconds
  send message "damage" to other
  if my Pierce is true
  stop this event
  destroy me
